                            "córka Idasa i Marpessy oraz żona Meleagra"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Ancient-Greek"
                        ],
                        "examples": [],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1.2\""
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "804a3be8-aba4-3790-a66d-ec74d030a857",
                        "entry_id": "d051d550-048c-36e4-9c7d-31b757dca8e7",
                        "glosses": [
                            "imię żeńskie"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ae4d5e73-a5ef-4d8a-96a6-50acdfeaa55e",
                                "sense_id": "804a3be8-aba4-3790-a66d-ec74d030a857",
                                "text": "Mam na imię Kleopatra i studiuję egiptologię na Uniwersytecie Warszawskim."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "68b3311c-bbdd-433f-8c47-365a950d4b17",
                                "sense_id": "804a3be8-aba4-3790-a66d-ec74d030a857",
                                "text": "7 stycznia, 1 lipca i 20 października przypadają imieniny Kleopatry."
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1.3\""
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "cc07e664-ee33-3c91-b915-048f9b4fcb2c",
                        "entry_id": "d051d550-048c-36e4-9c7d-31b757dca8e7",
                        "glosses": [
                            "planetoida o numerze katalogowym 216, z pasa głównego planetoid, odkryta w 1880 r."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "6807ed13-3794-422c-b6a5-6dd5fc4c2581",
                                "sense_id": "cc07e664-ee33-3c91-b915-048f9b4fcb2c",
                                "text": "Kleopatra porusza się w obszarze między orbitami Marsa i Jowisza."
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1.4\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ca9805e1-42df-4cb8-aaf9-7309f1f71089",
                        "source_entry_id": "d051d550-048c-36e4-9c7d-31b757dca8e7",
                        "source_sense_id": "804a3be8-aba4-3790-a66d-ec74d030a857",
                        "target_lang_word": "Kleopatra",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Kleopatra",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "464fb606-f172-320c-af38-6f754dc40b21",
                                        "entry_id": "18f4d0da-881f-34cd-9c45-ca7de9fc430a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Alternative spelling of Cleopatra."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "alternative"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c9a62658-bfe2-4866-b2a1-fcee05da7ed5",
                                                "sense_id": "464fb606-f172-320c-af38-6f754dc40b21",
                                                "text": "For a brief period the two Kleopatras, mother and daughter, ruled with the elder son, Ptolemy IX Soter II. The king’s younger brother Alexander was meanwhile based in Cyprus, while the queen who continued to rule with Soter II was probably Kleopatra III."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "90be910f-3e31-46b0-9627-f4bf730a3468",
                                                "sense_id": "464fb606-f172-320c-af38-6f754dc40b21",
                                                "text": "The famous Kleopatra was not done to death by an asp, as has been the traditional story; […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a360666b-6f41-44eb-a410-e655f1551094",
                                                "sense_id": "464fb606-f172-320c-af38-6f754dc40b21",
                                                "text": "Shortly afterwards Euergetes II raped Kleopatra’s teenage daughter, his own niece, but by 142 he had also married her, raising her to be joint queen along with her mother and so monopolizing all potential sources of dynastic influence. For us she is therefore known as Kleopatra III. Official royal protocol thereafter distinguished the two ruling Kleopatrai as “Kleopatra the Sister” (II) and “Kleopatra the Wife” (III) (though actually both were wives)."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "85585f4b-f87a-42be-bb17-a125578584df",
                                                "sense_id": "464fb606-f172-320c-af38-6f754dc40b21",
                                                "text": "The last section once again treats the Kleopatrai of Ptolemaic descent (203-208)."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "65e99844-b10b-42e4-869b-1d5eb9e2768d",
                                                "sense_id": "464fb606-f172-320c-af38-6f754dc40b21",
                                                "text": "The roles played by royal women in the Hellenistic royal houses were cast and re-cast by every generation of royal women stretching back to Olympias, the mother of Alexander the Great, but by the time these Kleopatrai stepped onto the Mediterranean stage the influence of such women was certainly nothing new."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8aeed611-ffd2-436d-aff3-988ab6907e4b",
                                                "sense_id": "464fb606-f172-320c-af38-6f754dc40b21",
                                                "text": "The three most famous films are highlighted here. Space prevents inclusion of additional well-known stage and filmic Kleopatras, such as the stage production of Cléopâtre (1890), staring Sarah Bernhardt, the silent film Cleopatra (1912), staring Helen Gardner, or Caesar and Cleopatra (1946), staring Vivian Leigh, which was based on the child-like Kleopatra of George Bernard Shaw’s play of the same name (1898). On the actresses who played Kleopatra in the cinema, see Wenzel (2005: 93-125)."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "3e9b94d4-675a-4e7e-80f6-b8600d35fff0",
                        "source_entry_id": "d051d550-048c-36e4-9c7d-31b757dca8e7",
                        "source_sense_id": "804a3be8-aba4-3790-a66d-ec74d030a857",
                        "target_lang_word": "Kleopatra",
                        "target_lang_code": "cs",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "62ef1d2f-4e61-4f68-a86a-707a9fdf1b85",
                        "source_entry_id": "d051d550-048c-36e4-9c7d-31b757dca8e7",
                        "source_sense_id": "804a3be8-aba4-3790-a66d-ec74d030a857",
                        "target_lang_word": "Cléopâtre",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Cléopâtre",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e9d00666-597c-3298-a8b2-349681908216",
                                        "entry_id": "763c8b93-82b9-3035-be91-36a563d731a2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Prénom féminin."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "23341bba-2ee6-419c-9976-e0ea997cdbb0",
                                                "sense_id": "e9d00666-597c-3298-a8b2-349681908216",
                                                "text": "Plusieurs souveraines d’Égypte et du royaume séleucide portèrent le nom de « Cléopâtre »."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ffd98366-0341-4b2b-99c0-cbf3917457ee",
                                                "sense_id": "e9d00666-597c-3298-a8b2-349681908216",
                                                "text": "Cela ne mène, peut-être, pas à grand-chose mais il est en tout cas certain que, si je dis « Cléopâtre », je pense tout d’abord à l’aspic caché dans un panier de figues (comme la plupart des gens, j’ai horreur des serpents), ensuite aux lions par lesquels elle faisait dévorer ses amants.\nJe pense aussi au mot « albâtre » — dont Cléopâtre a la pureté — puis j’évoque des images de portiques, de colonnes devant lesquelles se promènent les philosophes alexandrins — vieux pouilleux en guenilles — qui interfèrent dans ma mémoire avec ce que je connais de la moderne Alexandrie."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "37c52984-1864-46c0-a7b1-66355d9ab78e",
                                                "sense_id": "e9d00666-597c-3298-a8b2-349681908216",
                                                "text": "Les Bleues, elles, ont largement de quoi faire tourner : des cadres, comme Pauletta Foppa, Cléopâtre Darleux ou Laura Flippes ont été mises au repos en tribune, tandis que Grâce Zaadi ou Béatrice Edwige n’ont même pas quitté le banc."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "fe8f0da3-1390-44f1-96d0-a39f41c40906",
                        "source_entry_id": "d051d550-048c-36e4-9c7d-31b757dca8e7",
                        "source_sense_id": "804a3be8-aba4-3790-a66d-ec74d030a857",
                        "target_lang_word": "Клеопатра",
                        "target_lang_code": "ru",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Клеопатра",
                                "target_lang_code": "ru",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9a5e1b95-02ef-3aad-b854-ccf321f9b9b7",
                                        "entry_id": "0008488e-3fd7-388a-88c1-843fbfd0cdf7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "женское имя"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c5adda01-240b-4e23-9c12-c89e3cfcd094",
                                                "sense_id": "9a5e1b95-02ef-3aad-b854-ccf321f9b9b7",
                                                "text": "Мы имели в переводах сочинения св. Амвросия, Августина, Иеронима, Григория, Историю римских императоров (вероятно, Светонову), Марка Антония и Клеопатры; но Иовий укоряет нас совершенным невежеством в науках: в философии, астрономии, физике, медицине, сказывая, что мы именуем лекарем всякого, кто знает некоторые целебные свойства растений."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "89906e9b-61ef-463b-9a43-47d2abb0aff2",
                        "source_entry_id": "d051d550-048c-36e4-9c7d-31b757dca8e7",
